  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Mohanswaroop Khandelwal vs State Of Rajasthan And Anr on 28 April, 2017 High Court Of Judicature For Rajasthan Bench At Jaipur S.B. Criminal Miscellaneous (Petition) No. 2172 / 2017 Mohanswaroop Khandelwal S/o Shri Purushottam Lal, Age 43 years, B/c Vaishya, Proprietor M/s Mohan Trading Company, Shop No. 15-16, Airforce Circle Ke Pas, Sanganer, Jaipur (Raj.) ----Petitioner Versus 1. State Of Rajasthan through P.P. 2. Krishndatt Sharma, Food Inspector, (Headquarters) medical and health services, Raj. Jaipur. ----Respondent _____________________________________________________",
    "facts": "This criminal revision petition has been preferred on behalf of accused-petition challenging the order dated 19.04.2017 whereby application filed under Section 70(2) Cr.P.C. was rejected. On perusal of the documents annexed, it appears that the complaint came to be filed against accused-petitioner for the offence under Section 7(I)(iii) and 16 of Prevention of Food Adulteration Act, 1954, on which cognizance was taken against him vide order dated 7 rd August, 2007. The accused was summoned through bailable warrant. It appears that he remained absent on 5th May, 2014 and was called through arrest warrant.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that the accused (2 of 2) [CRLMP-2172/2017] has been facing trial since 2007 and because of serious ailment of his brother-in-law who was suffering from cancer kept him busy in regard to his treatment and could not remain present before the Court. Thereafter, he was called through arrest warrant. It is further stated that the report with regard to sample of 'Arhar Dal' has not yet been received from Central Food Laboratory. So no effective proceedings have been conducted against the accused- petitioner and the same has not been hampered because of the absence of the accused-petitioner. The facts stated by learned counsel for the petitioner are substantiated on perusal of the documents annexed with the petition.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for the petitioner submits that the accused (2 of 2) [CRLMP-2172/2017] has been facing trial since 2007 and because of serious ailment of his brother-in-law who was suffering from cancer kept him busy in regard to his treatment and could not remain present before the Court. Thereafter, he was called through arrest warrant. It is further stated that the report with regard to sample of 'Arhar Dal' has not yet been received from Central Food Laboratory. So no effective proceedings have been conducted against the accused- petitioner and the same has not been hampered because of the absence of the accused-petitioner. The facts stated by learned counsel for the petitioner are substantiated on perusal of the documents annexed with the petition.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
